# short-description: Create SD card image with 2 partitions for OMAP3 boards
# long-description: Laid out like the Debian 9.5 BeagleBoard-xM card image, which is known to boot on an xM. The boot partition is the only active primary FAT partition (type 0x0e) and holds MLO in its root, as the DM37x TRM (SPRUGN4S, 26.4.7.6.3) requires. The FAT parameters are the ones that image has (FAT16, 4 sectors per cluster, 4 reserved sectors, 64 heads and 32 sectors per track in the boot sector). The fixed size is a multiple of the 32 sector track so the filesystem is exactly as large as the partition, which the AM335x TRM checks for. omap3-sdcard.bbclass rewrites the MBR CHS fields to 255/63 afterwards. The kernel is told to mount the root filesystem ro so that the init system can fsck it, and it remounts it rw afterwards. wic writes extlinux/extlinux.conf itself (loader=u-boot) so root=PARTUUID names the root partition of this exact image: mainline omap3_beagle doesn't set the ${uuid} variable that the u-boot recipe's extlinux.conf relies on.
bootloader --ptable msdos --append "ro ${UBOOT_EXTLINUX_CONSOLE}"
part /boot --source bootimg-partition --sourceparams="loader=u-boot" --fstype=vfat --system-id 0x0e --label boot --active --align 1024 --use-uuid --fixed-size 32M --mkfs-extraopts "-F 16 -s 4 -R 4 -g 64/32"
part / --source rootfs --fstype=ext4 --label root --align 1024 --use-uuid
